  "query_preview": "..\n\nUpper ridging over the region will help maintain dry weather and\nclear skies through tonight. On Thursday temperatures will\nincrease ahead of a cold front with highs pushing into the 80s.\nAfternoon and evening humidity will drop below 20 percent for\nsouthern areas as winds increase to 10 to 20 mph, gusting to 30\nmph in the presence of dry fuels. Have upgraded the Fire Weather\nWatch to a Red Flag Warning in effect from Noon until 8 PM MDT\nThursday. \n\nA cold front will push through the region Thursday night with\nincreasing rain showers. Wetting rains are possible with the\nsteadier convection but will be fairly hit or miss. Look for\nmarkedly cooler temperatures over the weekend with highs only in\nthe 50s and 60s.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM and NBM90 were blended for Thursday wind to nudge toward\nhigher envelope of the forecast guidance ahead of the frontal\npassage and in support of fire weather highlights. Otherwise\nforecast used NBM which captured expected trends through the\nperiod. Confidence is above average for dry and windy conditions\nraising fire weather concerns on Thursday but below average for\ntiming and placement of specific showers Thursday night.",
